## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to translate regulatory constraints into practical, risk-balanced engineering decisions under time pressure, with an emphasis on STAR storytelling and real-world trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Data localization and privacy compliance
- Data flow mapping and architectural choices
- Trade-offs: latency, analytics needs, and operational overhead
- Rollback plans, auditability, and stakeholder alignment

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: data routing under localization constraint
function routeData(record) {
  if (record.country === 'in-country') {
    storeRegional(record);
  } else {
    tokenizeAndStore(record);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the chosen approach under regulatory audit requirements?
- What metrics would you monitor to ensure ongoing compliance post-release?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to navigate cross-functional disagreements with tangible trade-offs, focusing on privacy, latency, and customer impact. Shows facilitation, stakeholder mapping, data-driven trade-offs, and accountability mechanisms in a high-stakes setting common at Hugging Face and MongoDB.

## Key Concepts
- Stakeholder mapping
- Interest-based negotiation
- Mediation session design
- Trade-off formulation
- Feedback loops and postmortems

## Code Example
```javascript
function evaluateTradeOff(options) {
  // options: { privacyRisk, latencyMs, businessValue }
  // naive composite score
  return options.businessValue - (options.latencyMs * 0.1) - (options.privacyRisk * 5);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure success of the mediation after rollout?
- How would you handle a veto from a senior leader?

